# Shared agent policy

Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repo root for the Vite console, Go core, TypeScript, SOLID, theme, docs, and git commits.

Modular twins: [`.agents/rules/`](../../.agents/rules/) — `agents-policy.md`, `database-migrations.md`, `typescript-standards.md`, `solid-principles.md`, `theme.md`, `git-commits.md`.

Console lives in `packages/app`. The API and database live in `packages/core`. The tsnet proxy lives in `packages/edge`.

Non-negotiables:

- No secrets in git; no inventing infra/CDK/deploy unless asked
- `AUTH_SECRET` is required and fails loud; empty `DATABASE_URL` creates a SQLite file; local auth always on; incomplete OIDC disables SSO buttons only
- Product UI → `docs/theme.md`
- Commits only when the user asks → `git-commits.mdc`
- Schema changes are goose SQL in `packages/core/migrations` (`sqlite/` and `postgres/`)

TypeScript & SOLID details: `.agents/rules/typescript-standards.md`, `.agents/rules/solid-principles.md`.
